# Assertions checked during the replay, so an agent can verify its own work
# without reading a state dump by eye.
#
# What this run does: walks into the arena, clears all five enemies, is offered
# three upgrades from the seeded stream, and takes the second — which is `ward`,
# and holding it alongside `bolt` evolves into the Lance.

# Combat happened, and the pool was never exhausted.
tick 900 /Arena01 var:fired > 60
tick 900 /Arena01 var:dropped == 0

# Every enemy died, including the brute, which takes ten bolts.
tick 950 /Arena01 var:kills == 5
tick 950 /Arena01 var:enemy_count == 0

# The upgrade was taken and the run moved on.
tick 1099 /Arena01 var:room == 2
tick 1099 /Arena01 var:run_complete == true

# And the two spells the run holds evolved into a third. This is the assertion
# §12 asks for: a replay must reproduce the same spell evolution.
tick 1099 /Arena01 var:evolved == Lance

# The player survived to the end of the room.
tick 1099 /Arena01/Player exists == true
